    ]," she admits. "But we <b>are</b> still able to handle changes. Sometimes people move on their own, and sometimes people get resettled to build the numbers back up in places that have... lost people. But for the most part, people stay with their tribe. You vote with the tribe, pay taxes with the tribe, serve in the legion with the tribe. It's possible to get your place on the rolls changed and switch tribes, usually through marriage, but it's just an awful process and most people don't bother.

    "The other thing is the king's mercenaries, who sometimes convert their end-of-service bonuses into land grants or use them to build a home out in the village. Some of them even get citizenship grants for meritorious service! [serena.relationshipRange 1
        |After all, you've met little Matilda from my class;
